{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.TwoChannelTotalBindingFloor","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.TwoChannelTotalBindingFloor","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Log.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.reaching_target_forces_over_unit_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.reaching_target_forces_over_unit_sum","kind":"theorem","line":176,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/TwoChannelTotalBindingFloor.lean#L176-L204","doc":"**The obvious escape is closed, and closed in the opposite direction.**\n\nThe natural repair to reach for is \"the two isospin channels carry only a\nfraction `s < 1` of the trace normalisation — a spin or spatial factor the\ncolour-only fibre lacks — so the floor drops.\" **It does not drop; it rises.**\n\nUnder `μ₊ + μ₋ = s` the AM–GM cap is `μ₊μ₋ ≤ s²/4`, which *shrinks* with `s`, so\na smaller normalisation makes the product smaller and hence the total binding\n*larger*. Reaching any target below `α·log 4` therefore forces `1 < s`: the two\nchannels would have to carry **more** weight than the whole trace.\n\nFor a spectral projector decomposition of a single normalised trace that is not\navailable (`s ≤ 1` by construction — `InterfaceScalar.mu_sum_eq_one` has `s = 1`\nexactly). So this closes the sub-normalisation route rather than opening it: at\nthe substrate target the requirement is `s ≥ 1.547`.\n\nRecorded because the wrong direction is the intuitive one, and an earlier\nrevision of the companion probe asserted it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.no_t_odd_rescaling_reaches_target","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.no_t_odd_rescaling_reaches_target","kind":"theorem","line":162,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/TwoChannelTotalBindingFloor.lean#L162-L174","doc":"**No T-odd rescaling reaches a target below the floor.** Combining the two\nprevious results: the rescaling cannot change the total, and the total is floored,\nso every target strictly below `α·log 4` is unreachable for **every** `t > 0`.\n\nWith `α = E₀` the floor is `5.8030 MeV` and nature's two-nucleon total is\n`2.1510 MeV`, so this applies to the physical target. The ribbon-twist route is\nclosed without ever deciding what `f` is. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.convex_total_binding_floor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.convex_total_binding_floor","kind":"theorem","line":150,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/TwoChannelTotalBindingFloor.lean#L150-L160","doc":"**The floor.** For any convex pair of channel scalars and any positive\nenergy scale, the total binding is at least `α·log 4`.\n\nThis is where `μ₊ + μ₋ = 1` (`InterfaceScalar.mu_sum_eq_one`) does the work: it\nis not merely \"both channels bind\" (which follows from `μ_T < 1` alone) but a\n*quantitative lower bound on their sum*, which is what makes the comparison with\nnature decisive rather than qualitative. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.t_odd_rescaling_preserves_total","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.t_odd_rescaling_preserves_total","kind":"theorem","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/TwoChannelTotalBindingFloor.lean#L136-L148","doc":"**A T-odd rescaling cannot move the total.** Sending `(μ₊, μ₋) ↦ (μ₊·t,\nμ₋/t)` leaves `B₊ + B₋` exactly where it was, because the two `log t`\ncontributions enter with opposite signs and cancel.\n\nThe ribbon twist is the case `t = q^f`, so this says the total binding is\n**independent of the framing** — the quantity is blind to the one parameter the\ntwist route had to offer. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.total_binding_floor_of_prod_le_quarter","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.total_binding_floor_of_prod_le_quarter","kind":"theorem","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/TwoChannelTotalBindingFloor.lean#L125-L134","doc":"**The floor, from the product cap alone.** Isolated so that both the\nconvex case and the sub-unit case share it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.prod_le_quarter_of_sum_le_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.prod_le_quarter_of_sum_le_one","kind":"theorem","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/TwoChannelTotalBindingFloor.lean#L116-L123","doc":"The same cap under a *sub*-unit normalisation `μ₊ + μ₋ ≤ 1`. Carrying less\nthan the whole trace makes the product smaller, not larger — which is the step\nthat decides the direction of the escape in `reaching_target_forces_over_unit_sum`\nbelow. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.convex_pair_prod_le_quarter","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.convex_pair_prod_le_quarter","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/TwoChannelTotalBindingFloor.lean#L109-L114","doc":"**The convex product is capped at `1/4`.** AM–GM in the form that matters\nhere: a pair summing to `1` has product at most `1/4`, with equality exactly at\nthe balanced point. ","signatureChunk":0}]}